    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Lets admins renew posts by updating their publish date/time, resurfacing old content without manual republishing.</p>\n<h3>Source Code</h3>\n<p>Unminified JS and CSS source files are located in <code>assets/src/</code>. These are built using standard tools such as Grunt or NPM.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin files to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/wd-post-renew</code> directory, or install the plugin through the WordPress plugins screen directly.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin.</li>\n<li>Use the settings page to configure post renewal options.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='will%20it%20change%20the%20content%3F'>\nWill it change the content?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No. Only the post date/time will be updated.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='can%20i%20schedule%20post%20renewals%3F'>\nCan I schedule post renewals?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. You can schedule post renewals using WordPress cron jobs. Configure the renewal frequency and timing in the plugin settings to automate the process.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Automatically update post publish dates to make content appear fresh—ideal for news, blogs, and recurring promotions.",
